::id(doc-manifestDocRf)

=[Manifest Reference]

Generated by `catasto spec manifest` from Rust schema definitions in `crates/catasto-manifest/`. Do not edit it: change the doc comments there and run the command again.

Authoritative reference of all declarations and fields supported in `catasto.ctmt`.

==[upstream]

Upstream repository definitions declared in `::upstream(...)`. An upstream declares a named `catasto.git(...)` repository at a pinned revision, optionally with a `root` directory inside the repository from which entry paths start.

- `url` (string): Repository URL (`https://` URL or workspace-relative path), passed to `catasto.git(...)`.
- `rev` (string, default: `main`): Pinned tag, branch, or commit hash. Quote numeric revisions (e.g. `rev: "1.2"`).
- `root` (path): Directory inside the upstream repository that entry paths are relative to.

==[entry]

Manifest entry declaring a managed workspace file or repository. Each top-level entry in `catasto.ctmt` binds a workspace-relative path to a `catasto.{upstream,git,local,repo}(...)` constructor call; file entries may optionally pair the call with `executable` in a tuple `(call, executable: bool)`.

- `source` (catasto.upstream(...) | catasto.git(...) | catasto.local(...) | catasto.repo(...)): Constructor call declaring where canonical content comes from: `catasto.upstream(name, path: "...")`, `catasto.git(url, rev: ..., path: "...")`, `catasto.local("...")`, or `catasto.repo(url, branch: ..., submodule: ...)`.
- `executable` (boolean): Whether a managed file is placed executable (`true`) or not (`false`), whatever the source says. Left out, the source decides: a git file's `100755` or not, and a local file is never executable. Rejected on `catasto.repo(...)`.
